00:33:10,585 --> 00:33:18,630
And some people might just think that that building a company alone is is or doing something alone is is a sufficient contribution to society.
有些人可能只是认为，独自创办一家公司，或独自做某件事，就已经是对社会的足够贡献了。

534
00:33:18,680 --> 00:33:21,830
Creating a beautiful piece of art or all of it is true.
创造一件美丽的艺术品，这确实是真的。

535
00:33:21,880 --> 00:33:22,280
Correct.
正确。

536
00:33:22,320 --> 00:33:24,566
And so the question is what's the alignment?
所以问题在于，什么是契合？

537
00:33:24,616 --> 00:33:29,898
And it just depends on your background, your culture, maybe has something to do with where you live, where you came from.
这完全取决于你的背景、文化，也许还和你生活的地方、成长的地方有关。

538
00:33:29,948 --> 00:33:31,949
There's just infinite number of ways.
有无穷无尽的方式。

539
00:33:31,999 --> 00:33:35,110
And so my point is this.
所以我的观点是：

540
00:33:35,160 --> 00:33:37,270
Alignment is going to be a forever problem.
契合将是一个永恒的问题。

541
00:33:37,320 --> 00:33:38,150
Yes.
是的。

542
00:33:38,200 --> 00:33:44,190
If we depend on perfect alignment in order to ensure safety, then we're never going to get there.
如果我们依赖完全对齐来确保安全，那么我们就永远无法实现。

543
00:33:44,240 --> 00:33:46,230
And so the answer is this.
所以答案是这样的。

544
00:33:46,280 --> 00:33:54,550
The way we treat the way we think about babies and when we we're raising kids and you know, we have pets or whatever it is, employees.
我们对待婴儿、教育孩子，以及养宠物或管理员工的方式，都体现了这一点。

545
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:55,270
Okay.
好的。

546
00:33:55,320 --> 00:33:57,270
You start with containment.
你从隔离开始。

547
00:33:57,320 --> 00:34:02,769
You give them the rights that the access to tools, the access to information,
给他们使用工具、获取信息的权限，

548
00:34:02,819 --> 00:34:07,113
the access to whatever responsibility capabilities that they have, funds, resources.
以及他们所承担职责所需的资源和资金。

549
00:34:07,163 --> 00:34:11,105
You give them access based on the job that you ask them to do.
你根据他们被要求完成的工作来授予访问权限。

550
00:34:11,155 --> 00:34:13,244
You start out with zero trust.
从零信任开始。

551
00:34:13,294 --> 00:34:15,301
When you hire somebody, you start out with zero trust.
雇用一个人时，你从零信任开始。

552
00:34:15,351 --> 00:34:20,154
When you have a baby that's 1 year old, you put them in a playpen, you assume zero trust.
当你有一个一岁的婴儿时，你会把他放进婴儿围栏，假设零信任。

553
00:34:20,204 --> 00:34:26,839
And so you zero trust, you give them minimum rights and you expand that boundary as you learn more.
因此你要实施零信任，只给予最小权限，并随着了解的深入逐步扩大边界。

554
00:34:26,889 --> 00:34:31,096
And so when whenever we have a new AI, we have to assume the same thing.
所以每当出现新的AI时，我们都必须假设同样的情况。

555
00:34:31,146 --> 00:34:41,103
Whenever you're testing an AI, zero trust, minimum boundaries, minimum rights, and you expand it as you test and give yourself confidence.
无论何时测试AI，都要坚持零信任原则，设置最小边界和最小权限，并在测试过程中逐步扩展，以建立信心。

556
00:34:41,153 --> 00:34:46,230
So, containment, very tight containment is really important to any autonomous system.
因此，隔离至关重要，对任何自主系统来说，必须实现高度严格的隔离。

557
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:49,829
Second thing you do, uh monitoring.
第二件事，是监控。

558
00:34:49,879 --> 00:34:51,364
And the monitoring has to be out of band.
而监控必须是带外的。

559
00:34:51,414 --> 00:34:56,213
And the reason for that is because if you're if you tell an intelligent person, "Hey, listen,
原因在于，如果你对一个聪明的人说：“嘿，听着，

560
00:34:56,263 --> 00:34:59,070
I'm going to sit here and watch you do your work to make sure you're doing it right."
我就坐在这里观察你工作，确保你做对了。”

561
00:34:59,120 --> 00:34:59,710
Right.
没错。

562
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:00,670
Okay?
好吧？

563
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:06,664
And I'm going to sit here and watch you make sure that you're serving customers properly and that you're working hard enough.
我就坐在这里观察你，确保你正确服务客户，并且足够努力工作。

564
00:35:06,714 --> 00:35:07,470
Okay?
好吧？

565
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:12,230
That that autonomous system is going to behave differently than when you're not watching.
那个自主系统在你不在场时的行为会有所不同。

566
00:35:12,280 --> 00:35:14,990
It's like Brad's in the room with me or not.
就像布拉德在我身边或不在身边一样。

567
00:35:15,040 --> 00:35:15,748
Exactly.
完全正确。

568
00:35:15,798 --> 00:35:16,506
Exactly.
完全正确。

569
00:35:16,556 --> 00:35:17,011
Okay?
明白了吗？

570
00:35:17,061 --> 00:35:21,526
And so so the the the monitoring has to be out of band and it has to have the
所以监控必须是带外的，而且必须能够

571
00:35:21,576 --> 00:35:29,177
ability to observe that the autonomous system is doing something that was inconsistent with the policy or inconsistent with alignment,
观察到自主系统的行为是否与策略或对齐要求不一致，

572
00:35:29,227 --> 00:35:32,870
and you have the ability to either escalate or shut it down.
并且你有能力进行升级或直接关停。

573
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:33,220
Right.
没错。

574
00:35:33,240 --> 00:35:34,082
Just turn off.
直接关掉就行。

575
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:37,686
And so so those kind of capabilities have to exist.
所以这类能力必须存在。

576
00:35:37,736 --> 00:35:39,080
That's engineering.
这就是工程。

577
00:35:39,130 --> 00:35:40,322
That's technology.
这就是技术。

578
00:35:40,372 --> 00:35:41,274
And it's possible.
而且这是可能的。

579
00:35:41,324 --> 00:35:43,339
And we we announced it recently called Open Shell.
我们最近宣布了它，名为 Open Shell。

580
00:35:43,389 --> 00:35:45,974
We have, you know, over 100 100 companies now joining us.
目前已有超过100家公司加入我们。

581
00:35:46,024 --> 00:35:49,350
We've got lots and lots of activity around the world because everybody wants the same thing.
全球各地都涌现出大量活动，因为每个人都想要同样的东西。

582
00:35:49,400 --> 00:35:56,990
Starting at the highest level, you know, when I looked around the table at the White House, Yeah. um everybody around that table, right?
从最高层面来看，当我环顾白宫的会议桌时，是的，桌边的每个人，对吧？

583
00:35:57,040 --> 00:35:57,886
They're parents.
他们都是父母。

584
00:35:57,936 --> 00:35:58,729
They have kids.
他们都有孩子。

585
00:35:58,779 --> 00:36:06,510
I think there's this view in the country that there are some leaders of super intelligence that are just yoloing, that don't really care.
我觉得国内有一种看法，认为一些超级智能的领导者只是在盲目冒险，根本不在乎。

586
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:07,490
They're being reckless.
他们正在鲁莽行事。

587
00:36:07,540 --> 00:36:09,117
They just want to grab all the money.
他们只想攫取所有金钱。

588
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:16,803
And yet when I looked around their table that table, there wasn't a person in there that I saw that wants to be reckless, that wants to yolo.
但当我环顾那张桌子时，我发现里面没有一个人是想鲁莽行事、想盲目冒险的。

589
00:36:16,853 --> 00:36:22,990
In fact, everybody there wanted to find the right balance between fast and safe.
事实上，那里的每个人都想在快速和安全之间找到正确的平衡。

590
00:36:23,040 --> 00:36:24,502
That was the president's directive.
这是总统的指示。

591
00:36:24,552 --> 00:36:28,115
And I we we debated a little bit what that meant.
我们曾就这句指示的具体含义进行过一些讨论。

592
00:36:28,165 --> 00:36:28,565
Right?
对吧？

593
00:36:28,609 --> 00:36:32,140
There are different versions of how to implement that.
实现这一点的方式有多种。

594
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:38,870
But, you know, what would you say to the American public who fears that we have a reckless president or reckless leaders?
但你知道，面对那些担心我们有鲁莽总统或鲁莽领导人的美国公众，你会怎么回应？

595
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:40,302
Did you see any evidence of that?
你看到过这方面的证据吗？

596
00:36:40,352 --> 00:36:41,135
You have kids.
你有孩子。

597
00:36:41,185 --> 00:36:46,790
Do you worry about the future that you're bringing into existence with superintelligence?
你是否担心，超级智能正在塑造的未来会带来隐患？

598
00:36:46,840 --> 00:36:51,910
Safety and security technology Right. are part of AI.
安全与保障技术确实是人工智能的一部分。

599
00:36:51,960 --> 00:36:52,950
Right.
对。

600
00:36:53,000 --> 00:37:01,430
There's some weird formulation that AI technology and safety and security are orthogonal.
有一种奇怪的说法，认为人工智能技术与安全和保障是相互独立的。

601
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:01,950
Yeah.
对。

602
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:06,630
It's kind of like the airbags and the and the braking system Right.
就像安全气囊和制动系统一样。

603
00:37:06,680 --> 00:37:11,810
and the radars, the cameras, um the ABS, uh the the the lane keeping.
还有雷达、摄像头、ABS、车道保持功能。

604
00:37:11,860 --> 00:37:15,150
All of that technology is somehow independent of the car.
所有这些技术在某种程度上都独立于汽车本身。

605
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:16,310
Right. understand what I'm saying?
对，明白我的意思了吗？

606
00:37:16,360 --> 00:37:16,660
Right.
对。

607
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:18,910
The only thing that matters to the car is the engine.
对汽车来说，唯一重要的是发动机。

608
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:19,790
Right.
对。

609
00:37:19,840 --> 00:37:23,695
In fact, the whole car is part of the car's technology.
实际上，整辆车都是汽车技术的一部分。

610
00:37:23,745 --> 00:37:24,950
When I say Right.
当我说“对”的时候。

611
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:30,934
to accelerate AI's technology, what I mean by that is we need to accelerate the security technology.
为了加速AI技术的发展，我的意思是，我们需要加速安全技术的发展。

612
00:37:30,984 --> 00:37:33,163
We have to accelerate the safety technology.
我们必须加速安全技术的发展。

613
00:37:33,213 --> 00:37:35,310
They all have to be accelerated.
所有这些都必须加速。

614
00:37:35,360 --> 00:37:35,690
Right.
对。

615
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:39,352
If you ask me right now, I think everybody would say, "Let's accelerate security.
如果现在问我，我认为每个人都会说：“让我们加速安全。”

616
00:37:39,402 --> 00:37:41,325
Let's accelerate safety technology."
让我们加速安全技术。”

617
00:37:41,375 --> 00:37:43,550
Nobody says, "No, let's pace that."
没人会说：“不，我们放慢点。”

618
00:37:43,600 --> 00:37:44,070
Right.
对。

619
00:37:44,120 --> 00:37:45,519
We should accelerate that.
我们应该加速这个。

620
00:37:45,569 --> 00:37:47,730
It's all part of the same thing.
这都是同一件事的一部分。

621
00:37:47,780 --> 00:37:52,401
You can't separate capability, functionality from safety and security.
你无法将能力、功能与安全和防护分开。

622
00:37:52,451 --> 00:37:53,190
They go as one.
它们是一体的。

623
00:37:53,240 --> 00:37:53,870
Mhm.
嗯。

624
00:37:53,920 --> 00:37:58,455
And when you deliver the service, nobody's going to say, "You know, good good uh you know,
当你提供服务时，没人会说：“你知道，不错不错，你知道，”

625
00:37:58,505 --> 00:38:03,950
I I really like the the uh the functionality of your service, but boy, is it you know, wrecking havoc."
我真的很喜欢你们服务的功能，但天哪，它简直太破坏性了。

626
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:04,300
Right.
对。

627
00:38:04,280 --> 00:38:06,630
And so so I I think it's all one thing.
所以我认为这其实是一回事。

628
00:38:06,680 --> 00:38:07,050
Right.
对。

629
00:38:07,080 --> 00:38:11,359
And we treat it as all one thing, and and the industry has to treat it as one thing.
我们把它当作一回事来对待，整个行业也必须这样看待。

630
00:38:11,409 --> 00:38:16,980
And when we say accelerate, we have to mean accelerating the entire package.
当我们说加速时，必须是指加速整个体系。

631
00:38:17,030 --> 00:38:18,390
And right now Including the safety.
而现在，包括安全在内。

632
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:20,470
Including Right. especially the safety.
包括安全，尤其是安全。

633
00:38:20,520 --> 00:38:21,710
You mentioned pacing.
你提到了节奏控制。

634
00:38:21,760 --> 00:38:22,910
Especially safety.
尤其是安全。

635
00:38:22,960 --> 00:38:23,660
You know this.
你知道的。

636
00:38:23,710 --> 00:38:27,990
Some people read Pacing the Frontier by Dario um and thought that meant slowing down.
有些人读了达里奥的《掌控前沿》后，以为这意味着要放慢速度。

637
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:32,647
And I thought a funny moment in the room was when the president called on his new best friend Dario.
我觉得房间里一个有趣的小插曲是，总统提到了他的新朋友达里奥。

638
00:38:32,697 --> 00:38:34,506
He He referred to him in that way.
他就是那样称呼他的。

639
00:38:34,556 --> 00:38:39,190
And he said, you know, explain to me, you know, the your version of fast and safe.
然后他说，你知道的，给我解释一下，你对快速且安全的理解。

640
00:38:39,240 --> 00:38:45,950
And Dario started off by saying, "Mr. President, you said whoever wins AI wins."
达里奥一开始就说：“总统先生，你说过，谁赢了AI，谁就赢了未来。”

641
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:46,428
Right?
是吧？

642
00:38:46,478 --> 00:38:54,901
And he said that we're all speeding up, that they're speeding up, that they want to go fast, that they want to, you know, win the race with China.
他说我们都在加速，他们也在加速，他们想快点前进，想赶在与中国竞争中取胜。

643
00:38:54,951 --> 00:38:59,062
But also acknowledge that along the way we just, to your point you just made,
但同时，也必须承认，正如你刚才提到的，

644
00:38:59,112 --> 00:39:03,152
we have to make sure the safety systems are also speeding up and also keeping pace.
我们必须确保安全系统也在同步加速，保持同步。

645
00:39:03,202 --> 00:39:06,606
So, I thought that was an important moment where you had, you know,
所以我觉得这是一个重要时刻，你明白吗，

646
00:39:06,656 --> 00:39:11,078
because I think people have positioned him as though he's in opposition, right, to this.
因为我觉得人们一直把他当成与此对立的角色，对吧？

647
00:39:11,128 --> 00:39:14,916
But it seemed to me that you were all very much on the same page.
但在我看来，你们其实非常一致。

648
00:39:14,966 --> 00:39:22,371
You I You went to the cabinet room with him and and Greg and the other Frontier Labs to sign, uh you know, this agreement.
你和他、格雷格，以及另外几家前沿实验室的人一起去了内阁会议室，签署那个协议。

649
00:39:22,421 --> 00:39:26,534
Was there any chatter, you know, in that room about differences of opinion?
那个房间里有没有人讨论过意见分歧？

650
00:39:26,584 --> 00:39:29,374
Or was everybody, uh you obviously got it signed.
还是说大家都很顺利地签了字？

651
00:39:29,424 --> 00:39:31,146
Did anybody have to be put in a headlock?
有没有人需要被按住头？

652
00:39:31,196 --> 00:39:32,870
Or did everybody go willingly?
还是大家都心甘情愿地参与了？

653
00:39:32,920 --> 00:39:37,941
No, everybody was very very constructive, very productive.
没有，大家都非常建设性，非常高效。

654
00:39:37,991 --> 00:39:48,270
And um I I I think that that without exception, everybody um is dedicated to advancing the industry safely and securely.
我想，毫不例外，所有人都致力于安全、稳妥地推进这个行业发展。

655
00:39:48,320 --> 00:39:53,630
And the reason for that is because if it's not safe, it's not secure, the functionality will never get a chance to speak.
原因在于，如果不安全、不稳健，功能就永远没有机会展现。

656
00:39:53,680 --> 00:39:56,695
And so, the capability will never get a get a chance to shine.
因此，能力也永远无法得到彰显。

657
00:39:56,745 --> 00:40:02,137
And so, we have to We know that the priorities are at all times safety and security.
所以我们必须始终把安全与安保放在首位。

658
00:40:02,187 --> 00:40:07,470
Of course, recognizing that this industry came through a transition just recently.
当然，我们也意识到这个行业刚刚经历了一次转型。

659
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:07,850
Right.
没错。

660
00:40:07,880 --> 00:40:09,270
It wasn't but 6 months ago.
距离那件事才过去六个月而已。

661
00:40:09,320 --> 00:40:10,270
Mhm.
嗯嗯。

662
00:40:10,320 --> 00:40:11,670
This technology barely worked.
这项技术几乎无法工作。

663
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:12,190
Exactly.
没错。

664
00:40:12,240 --> 00:40:16,510
And so, the functionality and Without functionality capability, what's the point of making it safe and secure?
所以，如果功能性和无功能性能力都不存在，那让它安全和可靠又有什么意义呢？

665
00:40:16,560 --> 00:40:18,147
Nobody even cares about it.
根本没人关心它。

666
00:40:18,197 --> 00:40:23,261
And so the obviously the first the first job of AI is to to demonstrate it could do something useful.
因此，AI 的首要任务显然是证明它能做点有用的事。

667
00:40:23,311 --> 00:40:23,611
Right.
对。

668
00:40:23,634 --> 00:40:26,045
And it really reached that point 6 months ago.
而实际上，它在六个月前就已经达到了那个阶段。

669
00:40:26,095 --> 00:40:31,450
And so now it really wants to be deployed and and that and broadly deployed.
现在它真的渴望被部署，并且广泛部署。

670
00:40:31,500 --> 00:40:38,010
And so so there's no question that the industry the entire industry now has a has a strategic imperative,
因此，整个行业现在都面临一个战略性的紧迫需求，

671
00:40:38,060 --> 00:40:44,430
an incredible imperative, and great urgency to make sure that whatever we deploy is safe and secure.
一个极其紧迫的需求，以及巨大的紧迫感，确保我们所部署的一切都是安全和可靠的。

672
00:40:44,480 --> 00:40:49,944
And so I think I think everybody has completely convinced capable aligned functionality,
所以我认为，每个人都已完全意识到，必须具备可靠且对齐的功能性。

673
00:40:49,994 --> 00:40:54,453
capability, safety, security, they're all at exactly the same place.
能力、安全、保障，它们都处于完全相同的位置。

674
00:40:54,503 --> 00:40:55,744
Priority number one.
首要优先事项。

675
00:40:55,794 --> 00:41:00,870
And so so um I the question is winning.
所以，呃，我的问题是关于胜利的。

676
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:01,220
Yeah.
没错。

677
